# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clear Skies Forecaster — optional environment configuration
# Copy to .env.local and adjust. EVERYTHING here is optional: the map works
# out of the box with the keyless map types below. NEVER commit real keys
# (.env.local is git-ignored; this example file must stay placeholder-only).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time —
# restart `npm run dev` or re-run `npm run build` after changing them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Map type shown on first load. The floating Layers switcher inside the map box
# can change it at any time — swapping map types only replaces the <TileLayer>,
# so the view, overlays and observing pin are preserved.
#   satellite — Google satellite/hybrid imagery (mt1.google.com, lyrs=y), keyless   (DEFAULT)
#   dark      — Esri World Dark Gray (base + reference labels), keyless, dark theme
#   terrain   — OpenTopoMap relief (OSM data + SRTM), keyless
# Legacy provider names are still accepted and mean "dark"; they also control
# the head of the DARK chain:
#   esri  — Esri World Dark Gray first (default for "dark")
#   carto — CARTO Dark Matter; REQUIRES NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_API_KEY below,
#           otherwise the app warns and falls back to the keyless chain
#   osm   — OpenStreetMap standard tiles first, keyless (light theme)
# At runtime the ACTIVE provider is verified (tile pixel probe + tileerror
# monitoring); on failure the map steps ONCE to the next keyless fallback in
# that map type's finite chain (satellite → esri → osm, dark → osm,
# terrain → osm → esri), never retrying endlessly.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_PROVIDER=satellite

# Optional CARTO basemap API key (used only at the head of the DARK chain).
# Since late August 2026 CARTO stamps every KEYLESS basemaps.cartocdn.com tile
# with an "API KEY REQUIRED" watermark, so keyless CARTO is no longer used.
# If you want the original CARTO Dark Matter look, request a free key
# (5M tile requests/month, no approval queue) at:
#   https://carto.com/basemaps/apikey
# and set it here in .env.local. Leave unset/empty to use the keyless default.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_API_KEY=

# No key exists for the "Live clouds" overlay on purpose: it uses NASA EOSDIS
# GIBS geostationary Band 13 infrared tiles (GOES-East / GOES-West / Himawari),
# which are anonymous, watermark-free and refreshed every ~10 minutes. See the
# README for the coverage limits over Europe/Africa.
